<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Battle of El Alamein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-alamein">El Alamein</a> was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 1942 between British Commonwealth forces under Bernard Montgomery and the German-Italian army under Erwin Rommel. The Allied victory forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> armies into a long retreat across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> treat it as a turning point leading to the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s African colonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-el-alamein.jpg" alt="Second Battle of El Alamein" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Len Chetwyn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Alamein_1942_-_British_infantry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
